// An included file the global-statement parser stops reading before its end.
//
// 'recover' rather than 'reject' because the diagnostic is reported inside the
// included file, moduleeof.cone, and an inline annotation is only matched
// against the scenario's own source path. So the count and the exit status are
// what can be asserted here, and they are enough for what this is about: an
// include that
// ends early is diagnosed and stops the compile rather than silently truncating
// the file it injected.

include moduleeof

fn user() i64 {
  includedFine(1i64)
}
